# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles run inside Linux containers: always LF in the working tree, whatever
# core.autocrlf says. A CRLF run.sh builds an image whose entry point fails with
# "exec /app/run.sh: no such file or directory" (Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true).
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
# Datasets, fixtures and expected outputs are read byte for byte, and a \r is data (rules.md, CSV
# dialect), so git must never convert them: with core.autocrlf=true the fixtures fail on \r.
*.csv -text
*.json -text
